==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*20 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*8 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] spawns as the boss after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Protons, Neutrons, and Morons is similar to [[Blue Stone Desert III]], but now the Crustaceous Scissorex appears on a timer, not allowing the player to stall enemies. Bring [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] to deal with the relatively weak Metal peons and bring [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] for Wild Doges and chip damage. The stage is decently wide so you should have a lot of time for the enemies to run out or kill the boss.

The stage can also be rushed by killing the first few Metal Doges as fast as possible and then stall the enemies at their base by using a tanky, fast and cheap unit like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] while destroying their bases with a high DPS Cat like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

